<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mount Pelée</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Montagne Pelée</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mount Pelée is an active volcano at the northern end of Martinique in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-antilles">French Antilles</a>. Its eruption on 8 May 1902 sent a pyroclastic flow over the town of Saint-Pierre, then the island's commercial capital, killing about 28,000 people in minutes, with only a handful of survivors. It was the deadliest volcanic eruption of the 20th century and gave its name to the Peléan type of eruption.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mount-pelee.jpg" alt="Mount Pelée" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rehcral · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ville_de_Saint-Pierre.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
